  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Sasaki. Logic: rules.objective and rules.gameplay; climbing combinations and jata/kkota; team scoring by placement.',
    Player: 'Sasaki (44A) is a North Korean four-player climbing game with temporary partnerships (red 10 holders). Shed all cards by playing higher combinations or passing; team placement determines score.',
    objective: 'Get rid of all your cards before the others. Help your partner (the other holder of a red 10) when possible. Players are ranked 1st–4th by order of going out; team scores depend on placement.',
    gameplay: '1. Deal: 12 cards each from a fanned pile (no dealer). 2. Partnerships: Holders of the two red 10s are partners; one holding both plays alone. 3. First lead: Holder of Heart 3 (day) or Spade 3 (evening) may lead any single or valid combination. 4. Play: Counter-clockwise; each player must beat the previous play with a higher same-type combination (or a special combination) or pass. When three pass in a row, the last player to play leads. 5. Special combinations: Triplet, Sasaki (44A), Four of a Kind, Pig (two red 10s; beatable only by Black Pig). 6. Jata/kkota: A single can be beaten by a pair of same rank (jata); that pair can be beaten only by the fourth card of that rank (kkota). 7. End: When three players are out, the last shows any red 10s; scoring by team placement.',
    keyRules: [
      'Ordinary combinations (single, pair, sequence) are beaten by a higher same-type same-length combination or any special combination.',
      'Special combinations beat ordinary ones; Pig (two red 10s) beats everything except Black Pig (two black 10s).',
      'Running: Exposing a red 10 before play doubles the deal score; the other team may call stop to quadruple it.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Four players. Temporary partnerships: the two players holding the red 10s (Heart 10 and Diamond 10) are partners; if one player holds both, that player plays alone against the other three.',
      deck: '48-card deck: standard international deck with all Twos and Jokers removed. Ranks from high to low: A, K, Q, J, 10, 9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3.',
      equipment: 'Standard 48-card deck (no 2s, no jokers). Score sheet (optional). Table space.',
      dealing: 'No dealer. Cards are shuffled and fanned face down; each player in turn takes the top card until all 48 are taken (12 cards each). Play is counter-clockwise.',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. Deal: 12 cards each from a fanned pile (no dealer). 2. Partnerships: Holders of the two red 10s are partners; one holding both plays alone. 3. First lead: Holder of Heart 3 (day) or Spade 3 (evening) may lead any single or valid combination. 4. Play: Counter-clockwise; each player must beat the previous play with a higher same-type combination (or a special combination) or pass. When three pass in a row, the last player to play leads. 5. Special combinations: Triplet, Sasaki (44A), Four of a Kind, Pig (two red 10s; beatable only by Black Pig). 6. Jata/kkota: A single can be beaten by a pair of same rank (jata); that pair can be beaten only by the fourth card of that rank (kkota). 7. End: When three players are out, the last shows any red 10s; scoring by team placement.',
